Id: perm018w
Severity: WARN
Category: filesystem
Check: check_perms
Fix: chown root:root /.
References: chown(1)
Controls: CIS 3.3, 4.1; NIST AC-3, CM-6; ISO 8.3, 8.9; CE Secure configuration

The root directory '/' is not owned by root, or its group is not the
expected one. The top of the filesystem sets the tone for everything
below it: the wrong owner there can rename, replace or re-permission
system directories. Restore it with chown root:root /. (The ALERT-era
entry perm018a below is kept so old reports still explain.)
